  "review": {
    "book": "JDG",
    "entityID": "person:barak_401",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "She sent and called Barak the son of Abinoam out of Kedesh Naphtali, and said to him, “Hasn’t the LORD, the God of Israel, commanded, ‘Go and lead the way to Mount Tabor, and take with you ten thousand men of the children of Naphtali and of the children of Zebulun?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Barak said to her, “If you will go with me, then I will go; but if you will not go with me, I will not go.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "She said, “I will surely go with you. Nevertheless, the journey that you take won’t be for your honor; for the LORD will sell Sisera into a woman’s hand.” Deborah arose, and went with Barak to Kedesh."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "Barak called Zebulun and Naphtali together to Kedesh. Ten thousand men followed him; and Deborah went up with him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "They told Sisera that Barak the son of Abinoam had gone up to Mount Tabor."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "Deborah said to Barak, “Go; for this is the day in which the LORD has delivered Sisera into your hand. Hasn’t the LORD gone out before you?” So Barak went down from Mount Tabor, and ten thousand men after him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "The LORD confused Sisera, all his chariots, and all his army, with the edge of the sword before Barak. Sisera abandoned his chariot and fled away on his feet."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Barak pursued the chariots and the army to Harosheth of the Gentiles; and all the army of Sisera fell by the edge of the sword. There was not a man left."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 4:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "Behold, as Barak pursued Sisera, Jael came out to meet him, and said to him, “Come, and I will show you the man whom you seek.” He came to her; and behold, Sisera lay dead, and the tent peg was in his temples."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 5:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Deborah and Barak the son of Abinoam sang on that day, saying,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 5:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "‘Awake, awake, Deborah! Awake, awake, utter a song! Arise, Barak, and lead away your captives, you son of Abinoam.’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG 5:15",
        "textualBasisJa": "The princes of Issachar were with Deborah. As was Issachar, so was Barak. They rushed into the valley at his feet. By the watercourses of Reuben, there were great resolves of heart."
      }
    ],
